{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G5CLpYyoig5RrmbJQqrkkS","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce88d08d-e354-48ee-a9e8-a33d7aea2b51","uuid":"b99bbfad-2183-4574-907e-801682368d73","timestamp":"2026-06-11T02:50:59.052Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic","newString":"## sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant\n- Casualty copy keeps the original spell's targets (the \"you may choose new\n  targets\" option is not prompted) — deliberate simplification; the copy\n  mechanic itself is faithful and the copy is correctly not re-cast (E1 does\n  not re-fire for copies).\n\n## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic","originalFile":"# KEY_DECISIONS — SOS implementation run\n\nLightweight log of ambiguities, deviations from TODO.md, and deliberate\ncard-local engine limitations.\n\n## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic\n- Engine gap: `_resolve_spell` never consulted replacement effects for a\n  spell going stack→graveyard, and `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined but\n  never fired. Added both as small additive engine changes: a new\n  `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` consulted in `_resolve_spell`, and\n  per-attacker `AttacksTriggeredEvent` firing in `declare_attackers_step`.\n  Both are general (reusable) wirings of pre-existing event types, not a\n  one-card subsystem.\n- The \"may cast\" attack trigger auto-selects when exactly one legal target\n  exists (per TODO); with multiple, the controller chooses (None declines).\n  Declining a single legal target is not modeled — deliberate per plan.\n- The exile-instead replacement is one-shot, scoped to the specific spell\n  object, and self-unregisters when it fires. A countered free-cast spell\n  (which bypasses `_resolve_spell`) would not be redirected — edge case left\n  as a deliberate limitation.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":6,"newStart":3,"newLines":12,"lines":[" Lightweight log of ambiguities, deviations from TODO.md, and deliberate"," card-local engine limitations."," ","+## sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant","+- Casualty copy keeps the original spell's targets (the \"you may choose new","+  targets\" option is not prompted) — deliberate simplification; the copy","+  mechanic itself is faithful and the copy is correctly not re-cast (E1 does","+  not re-fire for copies).","+"," ## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic"," - Engine gap: `_resolve_spell` never consulted replacement effects for a","   spell going stack→graveyard, and `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined but"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
