{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LxuH1ssMgS4xn2QaLoH1Qd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H6ETiaSZ1HZatBLB8aNbg4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"## sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian","new_string":"## sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n- Loyalty-ability targets: extended `activate_ability` so the activation's\n  `targets` are exposed to the effect via `source.chosen_targets` (and the\n  StackObject), per TODO. Added a `targets` field to both ability-instance\n  dataclasses (defensive set for sources without `__dict__`). The −7 loyalty\n  requirement (≥7) is enforced by the engine's existing loyalty check.\n- Coin flip (gap): added `GameState.rng` (`random.Random`); −7 flips via\n  `rng.randint(0,1)`. Tests inject a deterministic RNG.\n- Skip turns (gap): −7 sets `target.skip_turns += heads`; `advance_phase`\n  consumes a skip when it would be that player's turn and passes it to the\n  other player (a bounded loop; equivalent to the old rotation when no skips,\n  so extra-turns/rotation engine tests are unaffected).\n\n## sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":421321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce88d08d-e354-48ee-a9e8-a33d7aea2b51","uuid":"84283444-63bc-498f-b1c1-0d693e7ddf58","request_id":"req_011CbvktFEdVXYTLNTni8XSw"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H6ETiaSZ1HZatBLB8aNbg4","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce88d08d-e354-48ee-a9e8-a33d7aea2b51","uuid":"5e598fbd-700f-4386-9296-706cb9f6bb40","timestamp":"2026-06-11T03:24:41.936Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian","newString":"## sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n- Loyalty-ability targets: extended `activate_ability` so the activation's\n  `targets` are exposed to the effect via `source.chosen_targets` (and the\n  StackObject), per TODO. Added a `targets` field to both ability-instance\n  dataclasses (defensive set for sources without `__dict__`). The −7 loyalty\n  requirement (≥7) is enforced by the engine's existing loyalty check.\n- Coin flip (gap): added `GameState.rng` (`random.Random`); −7 flips via\n  `rng.randint(0,1)`. Tests inject a deterministic RNG.\n- Skip turns (gap): −7 sets `target.skip_turns += heads`; `advance_phase`\n  consumes a skip when it would be that player's turn and passes it to the\n  other player (a bounded loop; equivalent to the old rotation when no skips,\n  so extra-turns/rotation engine tests are unaffected).\n\n## sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian","originalFile":"# KEY_DECISIONS — SOS implementation run\n\nLightweight log of ambiguities, deviations from TODO.md, and deliberate\ncard-local engine limitations.\n\n## sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian\n- Miracle (card-local): a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger tracks the\n  controller's first draw per turn with a turn-stamp on the card (the engine's\n  `cards_drawn_this_turn` is never reset, so it can't be used). On the first\n  draw of a turn, if it's an instant/sorcery, the controller may pay {2} and\n  free-cast it. A non-spell first draw still consumes the turn's slot.\n- The loot tests fire `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` directly — the exact\n  primitive `engine/turn.py` fires at the upkeep step — because `advance_phase`\n  (and thus `advance_to_phase`) does not run turn-based upkeep firing. This\n  exercises the real trigger logic; engine_tests already cover that the event\n  fires at upkeep.\n\n## sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n- \"Prepared\" is an SOS-custom keyword (no rulebook entry); its reminder text\n  doesn't say \"without paying its mana cost\". Ambiguous, but I followed the\n  build plan's explicit design (free cast via `cast_spell_free` from exile)\n  since the designer's intent governs a custom mechanic. `cast_prepared()` is\n  the card-local special-action entry point (no engine special-action hook).\n- ETB done in `on_resolve` (mirrors fdn_205). The creature is on the stack at\n  that point, so it's counted as +1 of \"your\" creatures for the prepared\n  comparison.\n- The Inkling token's \"white and black\" color isn't modeled (the engine has\n  no color attribute beyond mana cost); flying + Inkling subtype + 1/1 are.\n\n## sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone\n- \"Cast a copy from exile\" (Paradigm) is implemented by shallow-copying the\n  exiled original, marking it `_is_paradigm_copy` (so it skips Paradigm setup\n  and isn't re-exiled), and free-casting it from exile. The original stays in\n  exile as the permanent home; copies go to the graveyard. Reuses the\n  `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` seam (added for sos_1) to exile the\n  original instead of sending it to the graveyard.\n- \"First main phase\" = your precombat main; the recurring trigger fires on E2\n  whenever you're the active player (recurring, never unregisters).\n\n## sos_57 — Mana Sculpt\n- Added `card.mana_spent` (effective cost cmc) at cast time in `cast_spell`,\n  the \"amount of mana spent to cast\" a spell (parallels `colors_spent`).\n- \"If you control a Wizard\" is checked at the delayed trigger's FIRE time\n  (your next precombat main), per TODO — not at Mana Sculpt's resolution.\n  Delayed mana rides on E2; it self-unregisters after one payout.\n- \"Your next main phase\" is modeled as your next precombat main (E2 only\n  fires there). Casting it during the opponent's turn pays out next turn;\n  casting earlier in your own turn pays at that turn's precombat main entry.\n\n## sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n- Restricted mana (gap): added a separate `_restricted` track to `ManaPool`\n  plus an `allow_restricted` flag on `can_pay`/`pay`; `cast_spell` passes it\n  based on whether the spell is an instant/sorcery. Ability costs (the {5})\n  pay with `allow_restricted=False`, since activating an ability is not\n  \"casting a spell\". Unrestricted mana is spent before restricted.\n- Animation (gap): the land mutates in place (adds CREATURE type, Wizard\n  subtype, base 2/4, registers the pump trigger). `_reset_characteristics`\n  is overridden to NOT call super (which would de-animate by reverting\n  card_types) and to reset only the until-EOT pump. The EOT pump reset rides\n  on `EffectManager.apply_all`, which the engine runs during cleanup.\n- P/T while animated is exposed via `power`/`toughness` properties that\n  return 0 when not a creature (so a non-animated land isn't a combatant).\n\n## sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant\n- Casualty copy keeps the original spell's targets (the \"you may choose new\n  targets\" option is not prompted) — deliberate simplification; the copy\n  mechanic itself is faithful and the copy is correctly not re-cast (E1 does\n  not re-fire for copies).\n\n## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic\n- Engine gap: `_resolve_spell` never consulted replacement effects for a\n  spell going stack→graveyard, and `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined but\n  never fired. Added both as small additive engine changes: a new\n  `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` consulted in `_resolve_spell`, and\n  per-attacker `AttacksTriggeredEvent` firing in `declare_attackers_step`.\n  Both are general (reusable) wirings of pre-existing event types, not a\n  one-card subsystem.\n- The \"may cast\" attack trigger auto-selects when exactly one legal target\n  exists (per TODO); with multiple, the controller chooses (None declines).\n  Declining a single legal target is not modeled — deliberate per plan.\n- The exile-instead replacement is one-shot, scoped to the specific spell\n  object, and self-unregisters when it fires. A countered free-cast spell\n  (which bypasses `_resolve_spell`) would not be redirected — edge case left\n  as a deliberate limitation.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":6,"newStart":3,"newLines":19,"lines":[" Lightweight log of ambiguities, deviations from TODO.md, and deliberate"," card-local engine limitations."," ","+## sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer","+- Loyalty-ability targets: extended `activate_ability` so the activation's","+  `targets` are exposed to the effect via `source.chosen_targets` (and the","+  StackObject), per TODO. Added a `targets` field to both ability-instance","+  dataclasses (defensive set for sources without `__dict__`). The −7 loyalty","+  requirement (≥7) is enforced by the engine's existing loyalty check.","+- Coin flip (gap): added `GameState.rng` (`random.Random`); −7 flips via","+  `rng.randint(0,1)`. Tests inject a deterministic RNG.","+- Skip turns (gap): −7 sets `target.skip_turns += heads`; `advance_phase`","+  consumes a skip when it would be that player's turn and passes it to the","+  other player (a bounded loop; equivalent to the old rotation when no skips,","+  so extra-turns/rotation engine tests are unaffected).","+"," ## sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian"," - Miracle (card-local): a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger tracks the","   controller's first draw per turn with a turn-stamp on the card (the engine's"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
